WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.090 --> 00:00:05.700
In the Game of Thrones books, the most famous
noble families include the Starks, Lannisters,

00:00:05.700 --> 00:00:07.860
and Targaryens.

00:00:07.860 --> 00:00:11.380
But one of the most mysterious families is
House Dayne.

00:00:11.380 --> 00:00:16.779
Arthur Dayne was one of the greatest knights
in Westeros, but he mysteriously died – at

00:00:16.779 --> 00:00:19.199
the birthplace of Jon Snow.

00:00:19.199 --> 00:00:25.000
Ashara Dayne was a beautiful woman rumoured
to have loved Ned Stark, but she mysteriously

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:26.430
died.

00:00:26.430 --> 00:00:32.119
Darkstar is an edgy emo who may play a key
role in the ending of Thrones.

00:00:32.119 --> 00:00:36.680
Cause the Daynes have a legendary ancient
sword called Dawn.

00:00:36.680 --> 00:00:43.090
Their history stretches back thousands of
years , possibly to a distant empire of magic

00:00:43.090 --> 00:00:45.010
and prophecy.

00:00:45.010 --> 00:00:48.800
The Daynes live in Dorne, on the island of
Starfall.

00:00:48.800 --> 00:00:53.450
Cause according to legend, “the first Dayne”
followed a “falling star” to the island.

00:00:53.450 --> 00:00:58.780
There, he found a stone with “magical powers”
– the “heart” of the “fallen star”

00:00:58.780 --> 00:01:05.040
. And from that stone was forged Dawn, a strange
and “wondrous” greatsword . Dawn is incredibly

00:01:05.040 --> 00:01:11.020
sharp and light, but it’s not Valyrian steel
– it’s “pale as milkglass”, and “alive

00:01:11.020 --> 00:01:15.840
with light” . For thousands of years, Dawn
has been used by only the most “worthy”

00:01:15.840 --> 00:01:19.729
Dayne knights, who hold the title Sword of
the Morning.

00:01:19.729 --> 00:01:23.720
Most family swords just pass from father to
son, but to wield Dawn, you’ve actually

00:01:23.720 --> 00:01:27.530
gotta prove yourself, or else the sword lies
unused.

00:01:27.530 --> 00:01:32.400
So the Swords of the Morning are all famous
warriors in the history of Westeros, and “most

00:01:32.400 --> 00:01:38.039
famous of all” is Arthur Dayne .
Arthur was in the Kingsguard of King Aerys

00:01:38.039 --> 00:01:39.039
Targaryen.

00:01:39.039 --> 00:01:43.430
He was said to be its deadliest warrior , but
he was also famous for his chivalry , his

00:01:43.430 --> 00:01:48.279
sense of duty and honour . When he fought
against some outlaws, he first won over the

00:01:48.279 --> 00:01:54.399
common people . Then, he slew the villainous
Smiling Knight with his legendary sword Dawn.

00:01:54.399 --> 00:01:58.329
Arthur was also a tourney knight, winning
jousts and melees.

00:01:58.329 --> 00:02:03.359
Everyone who mentions Arthur admires and respects
him – Ned Stark calls him “the finest

00:02:03.359 --> 00:02:08.539
knight” he ever saw , and Jaime Lannister
idolised Arthur . Arthur’s the ultimate

00:02:08.539 --> 00:02:14.500
fantasy of a heroic knight in shining armour
– like the real-world legend of King Arthur,

00:02:14.500 --> 00:02:19.900
who also had a special sword that came from
a stone – like Dawn.

00:02:19.900 --> 00:02:25.250
Dayne was probably also inspired by Dane Whitman,
a comic book superhero knight with a sword

00:02:25.250 --> 00:02:28.610
made from a fallen star – like Dawn.

00:02:28.610 --> 00:02:33.370
Dane Whitman first appeared in Marvel Comics
in the 60s, when Game of Thrones author George

00:02:33.370 --> 00:02:36.920
Martin was a teenager – and a big comics
fan.

00:02:36.920 --> 00:02:43.370
In fact, Martin’s first ever published writing
was a fan letter to Marvel Comics in ’63

00:02:43.370 --> 00:02:48.569
. And now, in perfect serendipity, Jon Snow
actor Kit Harrington is set to play Dane Whitman

00:02:48.569 --> 00:02:54.560
in the MCU . So the point is that Arthur Dayne
represents two of Martin’s early influences

00:02:54.560 --> 00:02:59.859
– medieval fantasy and superhero comics
– stories about heroes.

00:02:59.859 --> 00:03:06.340
But Arthur Dayne is not the hero of Game of
Thrones – Arthur dies fifteen years before

00:03:06.340 --> 00:03:08.700
the story even begins.

00:03:08.700 --> 00:03:14.300
Because Game of Thrones questions and criticises
fantasy ideas of good versus evil.

00:03:14.300 --> 00:03:19.379
The death of Arthur Dayne is the death of
the simplistic noble hero, and the beginning

00:03:19.379 --> 00:03:23.030
of a more complex story, with more complex
heroes.

00:03:23.030 --> 00:03:28.959
But Game of Thrones doesn’t completely reject
heroic fantasy – and House Dayne is deeply

00:03:28.959 --> 00:03:34.980
intertwined with the series’ big mysteries,
and with the destiny of Westeros.

00:03:34.980 --> 00:03:39.639
In the Thrones TV show, it’s revealed that
Jon Snow’s parents are Rhaegar Targaryen

00:03:39.639 --> 00:03:41.120
and Lyanna Stark.

00:03:41.120 --> 00:03:45.130
The books haven’t confirmed this yet, but
it’s probably true in the books too.

00:03:45.130 --> 00:03:50.219
Still, the events surrounding Jon’s birth
are mysterious, and House Dayne was involved

00:03:50.219 --> 00:03:51.660
from the start.

00:03:51.660 --> 00:03:57.450
So, sixteen years ago , Lyanna and Rhaegar
ran off together to the tower of joy, guarded

00:03:57.450 --> 00:04:02.989
by three Kingsguard, including Rhaegar’s
friend Arthur Dayne . Robert Baratheon started

00:04:02.989 --> 00:04:07.200
a war against the Targaryens, Rhaegar went
to fight him and got hammered [got yeeted

00:04:07.200 --> 00:04:08.849
into the sun], and Robert became king.

00:04:08.849 --> 00:04:13.499
Ned Stark found the tower of joy, killed Arthur
and the Kingsguard, and his sister Lyanna

00:04:13.499 --> 00:04:15.720
died giving birth to Jon Snow.

00:04:15.720 --> 00:04:22.140
Then, Ned took Arthur’s sword Dawn back
to Starfall – and to Arthur’s sister Ashara,

00:04:22.140 --> 00:04:27.880
a “beautiful young” woman with “haunting
violet eyes” . We know very little about

00:04:27.880 --> 00:04:32.449
Ashara, but some characters remember her from
the infamous tournament at Harrenhal.

00:04:32.449 --> 00:04:37.580
This was the biggest party in Westeros – everyone
was there, and everyone wanted to hook up

00:04:37.580 --> 00:04:39.000
with Ashara.

00:04:39.000 --> 00:04:44.711
She danced with Oberyn Martell, and Jon Connington,
and she danced with a young Ned Stark, after

00:04:44.711 --> 00:04:49.800
Ned’s brother Brandon asked Ashara for him,
because Ned was shy . And there are rumours

00:04:49.800 --> 00:04:55.350
that Ashara and Ned fell in love that night
– that they shared “Words or kisses, maybe

00:04:55.350 --> 00:05:00.590
more” . In fact, some say that Ashara is
Jon Snow’s mother – which is probably

00:05:00.590 --> 00:05:03.850
not true – but someone did get Ashara pregnant.

00:05:03.850 --> 00:05:09.389
Cause according to Barristan Selmy, Ashara
gave birth to a stillborn daughter, and “soon

00:05:09.389 --> 00:05:12.139
after”, she committed suicide.

00:05:12.139 --> 00:05:19.400
After Ned came to Starfall, Ashara threw herself
into the sea, because “Her heart was broken”

00:05:19.400 --> 00:05:23.580
. Barristan thinks she may’ve killed herself
because of “the man who had dishonored her

00:05:23.580 --> 00:05:29.419
at Harrenhal” , and he implies that this
man was a “Stark” . So it sounds like

00:05:29.419 --> 00:05:35.479
Ned Stark got Ashara pregnant, but then he
married Catelyn instead, and he killed Ashara’s

00:05:35.479 --> 00:05:41.600
brother, and so Ashara was heartbroken . But
is honourable Ned Stark really the kind of

00:05:41.600 --> 00:05:44.450
person to knock someone up then dump her?

00:05:44.450 --> 00:05:49.120
Surely Ned would feel guilty if Ashara had
killed herself over him – but Ned never

00:05:49.120 --> 00:05:52.390
thinks about Ashara in his chapters.

00:05:52.390 --> 00:05:57.880
Barristan loved Ashara, so if Ned had “dishonored”
her, surely Barry would dislike Ned, but he

00:05:57.880 --> 00:06:00.250
doesn’t . It doesn’t make sense.

00:06:00.250 --> 00:06:05.259
So some fans believe that the Stark who hooked
up with Ashara was actually Ned’s brother

00:06:05.259 --> 00:06:06.259
Brandon.

00:06:06.259 --> 00:06:12.020
Unlike Ned, Brandon had a reputation as a
fuckboy , and he was “never shy about taking

00:06:12.020 --> 00:06:17.960
what he wanted” . He was older, more handsome,
more confident and more impulsive than Ned,

00:06:17.960 --> 00:06:21.000
so he might’ve been the Stark who got with
Ashara.

00:06:21.000 --> 00:06:25.480
The year after Harrenhal, Brandon was killed
by King Aerys, so grief for Brandon might

00:06:25.480 --> 00:06:28.449
have been part of what broke Ashara’s heart.

00:06:28.449 --> 00:06:33.479
But whoever her lover was, Ashara also lost
a stillborn child, and her brother Arthur

00:06:33.479 --> 00:06:38.370
died, and her companion at court, Princess
Elia, was brutally murdered in Robert’s

00:06:38.370 --> 00:06:39.370
Rebellion.

00:06:39.370 --> 00:06:44.360
All this horror and loss, and Ashara was probably
just a teenager at the time , so it’s easy

00:06:44.360 --> 00:06:47.180
to see how she’d be overwhelmed with grief.

00:06:47.180 --> 00:06:52.290
But the books never show us Ashara’s perspective,
we don’t know her thoughts and feelings

00:06:52.290 --> 00:06:57.780
– we only see her through the memories of
others, where she’s idealised and romanticised.

00:06:57.780 --> 00:07:04.090
She’s a symbol of a nostalgic past when
Barry, Ned and their friends were still young

00:07:04.090 --> 00:07:05.520
and full of hope.

00:07:05.520 --> 00:07:07.259
Arthur Dayne’s the same.

00:07:07.259 --> 00:07:11.940
When Jaime remembers Arthur, he thinks “The
world was simpler in those days”, “and

00:07:11.940 --> 00:07:17.830
men as well as swords were made of finer steel”
. Of course, the good old days weren’t really

00:07:17.830 --> 00:07:23.990
that good under Mad King Aerys, but in memory,
Arthur and Ashara represent a mythical bygone

00:07:23.990 --> 00:07:28.230
time when knights were honourable, and women
were beautiful , and there weren’t so many

00:07:28.230 --> 00:07:30.030
fucking white walkers.

00:07:30.030 --> 00:07:35.819
They represent the stories that George Martin
loved growing up, of heroic warriors and beautiful

00:07:35.819 --> 00:07:36.819
maidens.

00:07:36.819 --> 00:07:43.030
But the Dayne sigil is a “falling star”
, and when Arthur falls and Ashara literally

00:07:43.030 --> 00:07:46.240
falls, that romantic past falls too.

00:07:46.240 --> 00:07:52.400
It’s a tragic loss of innocence, [an original
sin], leaving a darker more complex reality.

00:07:52.400 --> 00:07:58.710
But there are hints that even Arthur and Ashara
were more complicated than they seem.

00:07:58.710 --> 00:08:05.090
In Book 3, Arya Stark meets Ned Dayne, the
twelve-year old nephew of Arthur and Ashara.

00:08:05.090 --> 00:08:10.099
His proper name is Edric, but everyone calls
him Ned , which is weird, cause Ned is the

00:08:10.099 --> 00:08:15.669
name of the man who killed Edric’s uncle,
and supposedly caused the suicide of Edric’s

00:08:15.669 --> 00:08:16.669
aunt.

00:08:16.669 --> 00:08:21.389
Edric mentions that he saw Ned Stark once,
and Edric doesn’t show any dislike for the

00:08:21.389 --> 00:08:27.770
man who supposedly brought death and grief
to his family . Shouldn’t Edric hate Ned?

00:08:27.770 --> 00:08:32.100
And Ned Stark doesn’t dislike the Daynes
– he thinks Arthur was a fine knight , and

00:08:32.100 --> 00:08:38.060
he brought Dawn back to Starfall as “a sign
of respect” . After everything that happened,

00:08:38.060 --> 00:08:41.680
why are Ned Stark and the Daynes so cool with
each other?

00:08:41.680 --> 00:08:46.820
Edric mentions a woman called Wylla who works
at Starfall . Wylla was Edric’s wetnurse

00:08:46.820 --> 00:08:49.180
– she breastfed him as a baby.

00:08:49.180 --> 00:08:55.720
And Edric says that Wylla also nursed Jon
Snow – so Edric calls Jon his “milk brother”

00:08:55.720 --> 00:09:02.290
. So this means that after Ned Stark killed
Arthur, and Ashara died, the other Daynes

00:09:02.290 --> 00:09:06.320
let Ned hang out at Starfall, while Wylla
nursed Jon?

00:09:06.320 --> 00:09:10.930
That seems very friendly to the man who got
two Daynes killed.

00:09:10.930 --> 00:09:16.250
Also, Edric Dayne and Robert Baratheon both
think that Wylla is Jon’s mother, which

00:09:16.250 --> 00:09:19.370
is probably a cover story to protect Jon.

00:09:19.370 --> 00:09:21.310
It’s all very confusing.

00:09:21.310 --> 00:09:27.870
But Wylla being Jon’s wetnurse, and Ned
Dayne’s name, and his attitude to Ned Stark

00:09:27.870 --> 00:09:33.590
all seem to suggest that Ned Stark and the
Daynes actually cooperated in some way.

00:09:33.590 --> 00:09:38.730
Starfall is fairly close to the tower of joy,
so it’s possible that Wylla was at the tower

00:09:38.730 --> 00:09:44.140
serving Lyanna while she was pregnant – Lyanna
was a teenager about to give birth in the

00:09:44.140 --> 00:09:46.320
mountains, she’d need help.

00:09:46.320 --> 00:09:50.940
So maybe Arthur Dayne suggested they get Wylla
from his family at Starfall.

00:09:50.940 --> 00:09:56.281
It’s possible that Rhaegar and Lyanna got
married at Starfall – the TV show says that

00:09:56.281 --> 00:10:00.960
they were secretly married “in Dorne”
. And maybe Ned Stark found out where the

00:10:00.960 --> 00:10:03.480
tower of joy was from Ashara.

00:10:03.480 --> 00:10:09.280
There’re all sorts of possibilities for
secrets and drama between Rhaegar Lyanna Ned

00:10:09.280 --> 00:10:10.730
and the Daynes.

00:10:10.730 --> 00:10:14.610
There are even theories that Ashara Dayne
isn’t really dead.

00:10:14.610 --> 00:10:19.880
We are told that Ashara’s body was never
found . So some fans believe Ashara faked

00:10:19.880 --> 00:10:25.100
her own death, and helped Ned cover up Jon’s
birth, and is now living in the Neck with

00:10:25.100 --> 00:10:29.170
Howland Reed, the last known survivor of the
tower of joy.

00:10:29.170 --> 00:10:34.660
Others believe that Ashara is secretly Quaithe
or Septa Lemore – which doesn’t seem likely,

00:10:34.660 --> 00:10:40.010
because Ashara has “haunting violet eyes”,
and Quaithe and Lemore don’t.

00:10:40.010 --> 00:10:44.970
But the whole situation is so mysterious and
ambiguous, that there must be some kind of

00:10:44.970 --> 00:10:47.650
secret amidst the tragedy.

00:10:47.650 --> 00:10:50.360
Arthur Dayne is also mysterious.

00:10:50.360 --> 00:10:54.570
Like, he was a Kingsguard, so what was he
doing at the tower of joy all year instead

00:10:54.570 --> 00:10:57.660
of guarding his king from Robert’s Rebellion?

00:10:57.660 --> 00:10:59.930
Why did he fight Ned Stark?

00:10:59.930 --> 00:11:03.680
Is Arthur really the noble knight we think
he is?

00:11:03.680 --> 00:11:09.650
Arthur was on the Kingsguard for Aerys Targaryen,
the cruel and terrible Mad King.

00:11:09.650 --> 00:11:14.740
Alongside Jaime, Arthur must’ve stood and
watched while Aerys burned innocent people

00:11:14.740 --> 00:11:19.620
alive . Was the heroic Arthur Dayne loyal
to this tyrant?

00:11:19.620 --> 00:11:24.170
In the years before Robert’s Rebellion,
Aerys’ court was divided into people who

00:11:24.170 --> 00:11:28.100
supported the Mad King, and people who preferred
his son Prince Rhaegar.

00:11:28.100 --> 00:11:33.490
It’s hinted that Rhaegar planned to overthrow
his mad father, and make himself king . And

00:11:33.490 --> 00:11:38.140
the worldbook says that in this political
conflict, Rhaegar’s “most formidable”

00:11:38.140 --> 00:11:44.230
ally was Arthur Dayne . Cause Arthur was Prince
Rhaegar’s oldest friend , Rhaegar trusted

00:11:44.230 --> 00:11:48.390
him with his secrets – and Rhaegar had big
secrets.

00:11:48.390 --> 00:11:54.040
Rhaegar was obsessed with the prophecy of
Azor Ahai, a hero prophesied to be reborn

00:11:54.040 --> 00:11:59.560
and save the world . Rhaegar believed that
his son would be Azor Ahai , along with two

00:11:59.560 --> 00:12:04.800
siblings , but Rhaegar’s wife Elia couldn’t
have any more children . So it seems that

00:12:04.800 --> 00:12:11.110
part why Rhaegar ran off with Lyanna and had
baby Jon Snow was to fulfil the Azor Ahai

00:12:11.110 --> 00:12:12.110
prophecy.

00:12:12.110 --> 00:12:16.610
And as Rhaegar’s oldest trusted friend,
Arthur probably knew all this.

00:12:16.610 --> 00:12:20.690
He was with Rhaegar and Lyanna when they went
to the tower, and apparently stayed with them

00:12:20.690 --> 00:12:25.990
for months . When Robert started the war,
and Rhaegar went to fight him, Arthur and

00:12:25.990 --> 00:12:31.070
the Kingsguard didn’t go and guard their
king, they stayed with Lyanna and her unborn

00:12:31.070 --> 00:12:36.970
son, presumably under Rhaegar’s orders . Cause
Arthur was loyal to Rhaegar’s prophetic

00:12:36.970 --> 00:12:42.080
mission, and loyal to Rhaegar’s son – the
future heir to the Targaryen dynasty, and

00:12:42.080 --> 00:12:45.450
possibly the future saviour of the world.

00:12:45.450 --> 00:12:50.550
But when Rhaegar died, and Robert beat the
Targaryens, the Kingsguard were in an awkward

00:12:50.550 --> 00:12:51.730
situation.

00:12:51.730 --> 00:12:56.451
They were stuck in a tower in Dorne, and Lyanna
was pregnant with Rhaegar’s heir, but they

00:12:56.451 --> 00:12:59.810
had no allies left, their side had lost.

00:12:59.810 --> 00:13:01.760
So – now what?

00:13:01.760 --> 00:13:05.260
[] In Book 1, Ned Stark dreams of the tower
of joy.

00:13:05.260 --> 00:13:09.530
He tells the Kingsguard he thought they’d
surrender – but Arthur Dayne says “Our

00:13:09.530 --> 00:13:11.170
knees do not bend”.

00:13:11.170 --> 00:13:15.260
Ned says the Kingsguard could run away like
Viserys and Daenerys – but the Kingsguard

00:13:15.260 --> 00:13:21.640
say they do not flee . Arthur and the Kingsguard
stayed loyal and defiant to the end.

00:13:21.640 --> 00:13:27.020
They refused to compromise, and chose to die
honourably, following Rhaegar’s last order

00:13:27.020 --> 00:13:28.800
to guard Lyanna.

00:13:28.800 --> 00:13:34.360
Of course, Lyanna at the time was dying in
childbirth and screaming for her brother Ned.

00:13:34.360 --> 00:13:37.550
All Ned wanted was to protect Lyanna and her
baby.

00:13:37.550 --> 00:13:39.540
And the Kingsguard wanted the same.

00:13:39.540 --> 00:13:44.140
So you’d think Ned and the Kingsguard could’ve
come to some agreement.

00:13:44.140 --> 00:13:48.880
Some fans speculate that Arthur faked his
own death, and is still alive somewhere, but

00:13:48.880 --> 00:13:51.180
there’s no solid evidence.

00:13:51.180 --> 00:13:56.900
Everything we know about Arthur shows he’s
a man of absolute loyalty and duty – “All

00:13:56.900 --> 00:14:02.720
knights must bleed”, he said, “Blood is
the seal of our devotion” . So Arthur bled

00:14:02.720 --> 00:14:09.190
– his noble inflexible honour led to his
death . The noble knight failed his Prince

00:14:09.190 --> 00:14:11.200
Rhaegar, and his King Aerys.

00:14:11.200 --> 00:14:14.310
But Arthur’s death still has meaning.

00:14:14.310 --> 00:14:19.900
Part of the prophecy of Azor Ahai is that
he’ll be reborn beneath a “bleeding star”

00:14:19.900 --> 00:14:24.700
. Arthur’s sigil is a star, and he bleeds
as Jon is born.

00:14:24.700 --> 00:14:30.330
The TV show highlights this, putting the star-forged
sword Dawn against the bloody bed where Jon

00:14:30.330 --> 00:14:31.630
is born.

00:14:31.630 --> 00:14:39.350
The magic of Azor Ahai is all about sacrifice,
and as Arthur Dayne dies, Jon Snow is born

00:14:39.350 --> 00:14:43.900
– a new heroic warrior to bring the dawn.

00:14:43.900 --> 00:14:48.910
In the TV show, the white walkers are defeated
by Arya pulling a sneaky on the Night King.

00:14:48.910 --> 00:14:54.600
But in the books, there’s foreshadowing
and prophecy that hint at a different ending.

00:14:54.600 --> 00:14:59.170
According to legend, thousands of years ago,
was the first Long Night, when the white walkers

00:14:59.170 --> 00:15:00.850
came for the first time.

00:15:00.850 --> 00:15:06.690
It was ended by the hero Azor Ahai, with a
sword called Lightbringer . Now, Azor Ahai

00:15:06.690 --> 00:15:13.310
is prophesied to be reborn, and to wield Lightbringer
once more . Melisandre thinks Stannis is Azor

00:15:13.310 --> 00:15:16.700
Ahai, so she gives him a fiery sword and calls
it Lightbringer.

00:15:16.700 --> 00:15:21.840
But Stannis’ sword isn’t the real thing
– Aemon says it’s “wrong” and “false”

00:15:21.840 --> 00:15:25.950
. Where is the real original Lightbringer
from thousands of years ago?

00:15:25.950 --> 00:15:30.100
Some fans believe that Lightbringer is the
Dayne sword Dawn.

00:15:30.100 --> 00:15:33.530
Dawn is unique, and mystical, and incredibly
ancient.

00:15:33.530 --> 00:15:38.480
It’s the only sword in Game of Thrones said
to be thousands of years old , and could date

00:15:38.480 --> 00:15:40.260
back to the Long Night.

00:15:40.260 --> 00:15:45.770
And it’s called Dawn – the Long Night
ended in the War for the Dawn.

00:15:45.770 --> 00:15:52.520
It’s about light overcoming darkness, and
Dawn is forged from a fallen star, it’s

00:15:52.520 --> 00:15:54.390
“alive with light”.

00:15:54.390 --> 00:15:58.960
So the symbolism and the timeline both make
sense for Dawn to be the original Lightbringer.

00:15:58.960 --> 00:16:04.470
But Lightbringer is said to be a “burning
sword” , and Dawn isn’t fiery.

00:16:04.470 --> 00:16:10.320
So maybe Dawn will become fiery after a sacrifice
– like how Beric’s sword takes fire from

00:16:10.320 --> 00:16:15.370
his blood . It’s said that Lightbringer
was forged with the sacrifice of Azor Ahai’s

00:16:15.370 --> 00:16:20.590
wife Nissa Nissa – he stabbed her with Lightbringer,
and “her soul and her strength” “went

00:16:20.590 --> 00:16:26.440
into the steel” . So maybe Jon Snow will
sacrifice his love Daenerys using Dawn, and

00:16:26.440 --> 00:16:32.100
her fiery soul will go into the sword, and
reignite it to become Lightbringer.

00:16:32.100 --> 00:16:37.640
That way, instead of Daenerys’ death being
like putting down a rabid fascist dog, her

00:16:37.640 --> 00:16:42.670
death could be a tragic sacrifice to bring
light against the darkness.

00:16:42.670 --> 00:16:45.850
Dawn might be the sword that will save the
world.

00:16:45.850 --> 00:16:50.470
But currently, Dawn is in Starfall, waiting
for a “knight of House Dayne” to become

00:16:50.470 --> 00:16:55.210
Sword of the Morning . Jon’s not a Dayne
knight, so he can’t go take it.

00:16:55.210 --> 00:16:58.540
Who will bring Dawn into the story?

00:16:58.540 --> 00:17:04.010
When Arya meets Edric Dayne in Book 3, he’s
twelve years old , serving Beric Dondarrion

00:17:04.010 --> 00:17:09.519
as a squire . Edric is a shy , “polite”
kid, and doesn’t seem like much of a warrior

00:17:09.519 --> 00:17:14.069
. But when George Martin introduced Edric,
he might have been planning for him to become

00:17:14.069 --> 00:17:15.419
the Sword of the Morning.

00:17:15.419 --> 00:17:20.589
Cause at the time, Martin’s plan was for
Book 4 to begin five years after the end of

00:17:20.589 --> 00:17:21.589
Book 3.

00:17:21.589 --> 00:17:26.069
Meaning, the characters in Book 4 would all
be five years older – Bran would’ve spent

00:17:26.069 --> 00:17:30.929
five years learning magic with Bloodraven,
and Arya would’ve spent five years in Braavos.

00:17:30.929 --> 00:17:35.950
Cause lots of characters are really young
in the books, and the five year gap would’ve

00:17:35.950 --> 00:17:39.660
aged them up, made them older and more experienced
for the later story.

00:17:39.660 --> 00:17:44.029
But Martin found that the gap didn’t work
for some storylines, and it sucked to use

00:17:44.029 --> 00:17:46.789
flashbacks to explain the last five years.

00:17:46.789 --> 00:17:51.529
So he scrapped the gap, and wrote Book 4 to
just continue where Book 3 left off.

00:17:51.529 --> 00:17:56.759
So some characters are still really young
– in Book 4, Arya’s just eleven years

00:17:56.759 --> 00:18:01.730
old when she starts assassinating people , and
Rickon is just four , so he can barely be

00:18:01.730 --> 00:18:07.200
in the story . Removing the five-year gap
forced Martin to change his plans.

00:18:07.200 --> 00:18:10.409
And this might have affected young Edric Dayne.

00:18:10.409 --> 00:18:14.029
If he spent five years with Beric’s men
in the riverlands, he could’ve grown up

00:18:14.029 --> 00:18:18.070
into seventeen-year old warrior worthy of
wielding Dawn.

00:18:18.070 --> 00:18:22.720
But since Martin removed the gap, Edric stayed
twelve, and he doesn’t even appear after

00:18:22.720 --> 00:18:24.039
Book 3.

00:18:24.039 --> 00:18:27.600
But in Book 4, a new Dayne character is introduced.

00:18:27.600 --> 00:18:31.370
A warrior with the skill and age to potentially
wield Dawn.

00:18:31.370 --> 00:18:34.799
But this character’s not as friendly as
Edric.

00:18:34.799 --> 00:18:41.369
His name is Gerold Dayne, but men call him
“Darkstar”, and he is “of the night”

00:18:41.369 --> 00:18:47.330
. Darkstar is a tryhard emo edgelord who wants
everyone to know how dark and brooding he

00:18:47.330 --> 00:18:48.330
is.

00:18:48.330 --> 00:18:53.269
He’s arrogant and violent and cruel – he
cuts off Myrcella’s ear during Arianne’s

00:18:53.269 --> 00:18:55.550
plot, it’s a whole thing.

00:18:55.550 --> 00:19:01.070
By Book 5, Darkstar goes to High Hermitage
– a castle right by Starfall, where Dawn

00:19:01.070 --> 00:19:02.130
is.

00:19:02.130 --> 00:19:05.170
Fans speculate that he might steal his family’s
sword.

00:19:05.170 --> 00:19:10.100
Cause Darkstar is jealous of his famous cousin
Arthur . He says the only reason Arthur was

00:19:10.100 --> 00:19:15.110
a “great knight” is cause he had the “great
sword” Dawn – it sounds like Darkstar

00:19:15.110 --> 00:19:20.700
wants Dawn for himself, to prove himself better
than Arthur – perhaps a Sword of the Evening,

00:19:20.700 --> 00:19:23.210
to rival the Sword of the Morning.

00:19:23.210 --> 00:19:27.360
If Darkstar gets Dawn, he could take over
whatever plotline was meant for Edric before

00:19:27.360 --> 00:19:29.600
the five year gap was scrapped.

00:19:29.600 --> 00:19:34.409
Once Dawn is back in the story, it could find
its way into the hands of Jon Snow, or whoever

00:19:34.409 --> 00:19:35.929
else plays the role of Azor Ahai.

00:19:35.929 --> 00:19:37.133
Then Dawn can be Lightbringer, and drive back
the darkness once more.

00:19:37.133 --> 00:19:41.950
Cause the connections between House Dayne
and the legends of Azor Ahai go way back into

00:19:41.950 --> 00:19:46.070
ancient history, and to a far distant empire.

00:19:46.070 --> 00:19:49.179
When Arya meets Edric, she’s surprised by
his appearance.

00:19:49.179 --> 00:19:54.019
Cause the Daynes are from Dorne, and Arya
thinks Dornishmen have dark hair and dark

00:19:54.019 --> 00:19:55.019
eyes.

00:19:55.019 --> 00:20:00.720
But Edric has “pale blond” hair and blue
eyes that look “almost purple” . Darkstar

00:20:00.720 --> 00:20:06.850
has “silver” blond hair and “purple”
eyes . And Ashara Dayne famously has “haunting

00:20:06.850 --> 00:20:07.850
purple eyes”.

00:20:07.850 --> 00:20:10.290
Arthur’s appearance isn’t described.

00:20:10.290 --> 00:20:16.499
But all of the known Daynes have eyes described
as purple, and most have pale blond hair.

00:20:16.499 --> 00:20:20.330
Purple eyes and blond hair are associated
with the Targaryens.

00:20:20.330 --> 00:20:24.800
The TV show doesn’t do the purple eyes,
but in the books, Daenerys and her family

00:20:24.800 --> 00:20:31.460
famously have purple eyes and blond hair . Because
the Targaryens descend from Valyria, the ancient

00:20:31.460 --> 00:20:33.950
empire of the dragonlords.

00:20:33.950 --> 00:20:39.340
Purple eyes and blond hair indicate “the
blood of the dragon”, the Valyrian lineage

00:20:39.340 --> 00:20:45.409
of dragonriding and fire magic . Every character
in Game of Thrones with purple eyes is a either

00:20:45.409 --> 00:20:50.389
a Targaryen or has some Valyrian blood – except
for the Daynes.

00:20:50.389 --> 00:20:55.950
Cause the Daynes were in Westeros thousands
of years before the Valyrians arrived . So

00:20:55.950 --> 00:20:59.409
where did the Daynes get their special purple
eyes?

00:20:59.409 --> 00:21:03.330
There’s another weird anachronism nearby
to Starfall.

00:21:03.330 --> 00:21:07.960
In the city of Oldtown is the Hightower, the
tallest tower in Westeros.

00:21:07.960 --> 00:21:13.860
The Hightower was built on top of a much older
fortress made of fused black stone.

00:21:13.860 --> 00:21:18.210
Fused black stone is made with dragonfire,
so you’d think this structure was built

00:21:18.210 --> 00:21:24.769
by Valyrian dragonriders . But maesters say
that the architecture is “singularly un-Valyrian”

00:21:24.769 --> 00:21:30.409
– it must have been built by some other
people who came to Westeros with dragons thousands

00:21:30.409 --> 00:21:32.980
of years before the Valyrians.

00:21:32.980 --> 00:21:36.850
So who are these mysterious ancient dragonriders?

00:21:36.850 --> 00:21:42.919
Could they be the purple-eyed ancestors of
both the Daynes and the Valyrians ? According

00:21:42.919 --> 00:21:48.360
to legend, in the far far east was the Great
Empire of the Dawn.

00:21:48.360 --> 00:21:53.190
Thousands of years before Valyria and Westeros,
it was the most advanced and prosperous empire

00:21:53.190 --> 00:21:57.940
in the world – until the reign of the Bloodstone
Emperor.

00:21:57.940 --> 00:22:03.179
He worshipped “a black stone that had fallen
from the sky” , which sounds like the Dayne

00:22:03.179 --> 00:22:04.970
legend of the fallen star.

00:22:04.970 --> 00:22:10.909
And the Bloodstone Emperor killed his sister
the Amethyst Empress – amethysts are purple,

00:22:10.909 --> 00:22:12.539
like Dayne eyes.

00:22:12.539 --> 00:22:18.340
And apparently, this caused the Long Night
, which was ended by Azor Ahai with Lightbringer

00:22:18.340 --> 00:22:25.019
. To defend the Empire, the massive Five Forts
were built , which seems a lot like the Wall.

00:22:25.019 --> 00:22:29.950
So this legend sounds just like the story
of the Long Night in Westeros , except the

00:22:29.950 --> 00:22:34.720
Great Empire of the Dawn is on the opposite
side of the world to Westeros.

00:22:34.720 --> 00:22:40.039
How did Azor Ahai defeat the darkness in Essos
and in distant Westeros?

00:22:40.039 --> 00:22:42.600
The answer might be dragons.

00:22:42.600 --> 00:22:49.620
Cause the Five Forts, like the Hightower fortress,
are made of fused black stone , so the Great

00:22:49.620 --> 00:22:52.179
Empire must’ve had dragons.

00:22:52.179 --> 00:22:56.740
Maybe after Azor Ahai defeated the darkness
in the east, he flew over to Westeros and

00:22:56.740 --> 00:22:58.620
ended the Long Night there.

00:22:58.620 --> 00:23:02.120
He could’ve built the mysterious Hightower
fortress.

00:23:02.120 --> 00:23:07.539
He could’ve founded House Dayne, and renamed
his sword Lightbringer to Dawn, and started

00:23:07.539 --> 00:23:11.450
the tradition of the Swords of the Morning
to keep his descendants ready for the next

00:23:11.450 --> 00:23:12.789
Long Night.

00:23:12.789 --> 00:23:17.461
Maybe House Dayne is the ancient lineage of
Azor Ahai of the Great Empire of the Dawn,

00:23:17.461 --> 00:23:22.509
the hero destined to be reborn and save the
world from darkness.

00:23:22.509 --> 00:23:28.840
And thing is, both Jon Snow and Daenerys have
a Dayne ancestor, Dyanna Dayne.

00:23:28.840 --> 00:23:33.909
Daenerys hatches her dragons beneath a bleeding
star, like the Dayne sigil.

00:23:33.909 --> 00:23:39.620
She has a dream of ghostly kings with “swords
of pale fire” and “amethyst” eyes , which

00:23:39.620 --> 00:23:42.630
might symbolise the Great Empire of the Dawn.

00:23:42.630 --> 00:23:47.460
And the whole story of Jon’s mysterious
birth is intertwined with the fall of Arthur

00:23:47.460 --> 00:23:49.179
and Ashara Dayne.

00:23:49.179 --> 00:23:53.679
In Book 3, Jon looks up at a constellation
called “The Sword of the Morning”, and

00:23:53.679 --> 00:23:58.610
“the bright white star in its hilt” blazes
“like a diamond in the dawn” – and he

00:23:58.610 --> 00:24:04.929
allows himself to “hope” . The fall of
Arthur and Ashara Dayne wasn’t for nothing,

00:24:04.929 --> 00:24:08.750
and the fantasy ideals they represent aren’t
dead yet.

00:24:08.750 --> 00:24:14.080
Cause they led to the rise of new heroes,
who carry on their ancient legacy to fulfil

00:24:14.080 --> 00:24:16.320
prophecy and bring light.

00:24:16.320 --> 00:24:22.390
After the night comes dawn, to defeat the
darkness once more.

00:24:22.390 --> 00:24:25.880
If you wanna know more about the mysteries
of Game of Thrones, you’ve gotta check out

00:24:25.880 --> 00:24:26.880
